data url back: 4×3 webp
source: 40×30 png
lossless
same each time
a 30000×30000 PNG: Image::fromBase64(): the image is too large: images may have at most 16,384 pixels a side and 50,000,000 pixels
not an image: Image::fromBase64(): not a PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP image
not base64: Image::fromBase64(): the text is not Base64
a cut PNG: Image::fromBase64(): the PNG image is damaged or not supported (unexpected end of file)
fit 0: fit(): the width must be at least 1, not 0
resize too large: resize(): 20000×10 is not a size an image may have: images may have at most 16,384 pixels a side and 50,000,000 pixels
too many pixels: resize(): 10000×10000 is not a size an image may have: images may have at most 16,384 pixels a side and 50,000,000 pixels
crop outside: crop(): the part 10×10 at (35, 0) is not inside the image of 40×30
rotate 45: rotate(): 45 is not a multiple of 90 degrees
gif: toBase64(): GIF is not written; use "png"
bmp: toBase64(): unknown format "bmp" ("png", "jpeg" or "webp")
quality 0: toBase64(): the quality must be 1 to 100, not 0
quality 101: toBase64(): the quality must be 1 to 100, not 101
saveTo: write access to "out.png" is not allowed; keep files in a directory listed in [permissions].write in phv.toml (e.g. "data/")
open: read access to "photo.jpg" is not allowed; keep files in a directory listed in [permissions].read in phv.toml (e.g. "data/")
